Mystery Word Game
A command-line word guessing game built with Python. The game selects a word at random, and the player guesses it one letter at a time. After an incorrect guess, it displays a hint for the selected word.
Features
- Random word selection from a word-and-hint dictionary
- Displays the number of letters in the word
- Reveals correctly guessed letters
- Shows a hint after an incorrect guess
- Tracks incorrect guesses and remaining attempts
- Validates guesses and detects repeated letters
- Offers another round after each game
Requirements
- Python 3
- No external packages
Run the Game
Save the code as mystery_word_game.py, then run:
python mystery_word_game.py
How to Play
1. Enter one letter when prompted.
2. Correct guesses reveal that letter in the word.
3. Incorrect guesses use one attempt and display a hint.
4. Guess the full word before you run out of attempts.
5. Choose whether to play another round.
